<div class="article-content">
  <h2>Why Is Accurate Date Arithmetic Essential?</h2>
  <p>Accurate date arithmetic is a fundamental requirement across project planning, legal agreements, financial forecasting, and personal scheduling. Counting days manually on a calendar often leads to errors due to variable month lengths, weekend overlaps, and leap days. Utilizing automated client-side date arithmetic ensures exact calendar placement every time.</p>

  <h2>How Business Day Filtering Works</h2>
  <p>When planning business operations, standard calendar days often fail to reflect actual working timelines. Project deliverables, payment terms, and legal notice periods routinely specify business days. When the business days filter is active, the calculator skips Saturdays and Sundays, ensuring deadlines accurately reflect actual operational business days.</p>
